                <pb facs="0453" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/12–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-18T14:00:00+03:25">December 18,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>936. My 932, December 15. Medjliss Finance Committee has approved proposal to
                    take away from Millspaugh the economic powers granted by the law of 13
                    Ordibehesht. The committee is still undecided regarding the clause in the Prime
                    Minister’s bill providing that these powers be vested in the Government. It
                    seems to be realized that they cannot be completely abolished and various
                    suggestions are under consideration including the creation of a Ministry of
                    Economics or alternatively a special committee which would be given authority to
                    conduct the emergency economic operations now under Millspaugh’s direction.
                    There is as yet no indication as to when the committee will report the bill back
                    to the assembly.</p>
                <p>Yesterday’s newspapers published text of letter Millspaugh has written Medjliss
                    President in which he asserted that repeal of powers would be harmful to Iran
                    and consequences. He concluded however by saying he hoped the Government would
                    be successful in its efforts to reorganize economic administration and declared
                    himself ready to cooperate within the scope of his financial powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
